   'A2 · 雙11的話 · Double 11 words'
   'Double 11 gives you four useful words: 清單 (shopping list), 實付金額 (the final amount you pay), 領券 (claiming coupons) and 鑑賞期 (the cooling-off period). Learn them once, and every sale makes sense.'
   'Four Double 11 words: 清單, 實付金額, 領券, 鑑賞期.'
   '清單 is the list you write before you shop. 實付金額 is what you actually pay after discounts. 領券 means claiming a coupon before it runs out. 鑑賞期 is the 7 days after delivery when you can return most goods.'
   'Claim coupons before they run out.'
   "Practise: 「我的購物清單是什麼？」 ('What is on my shopping list?') — write it first, then compare prices."
   'B1 · 影展與鋼雕 · Film & steel'
   "Film and steel share this week's headlines. Group the words and they stick: film （入圍、頒獎、星光大道） and steel （鋼雕、保險箱、勞動記憶）."
   'Group the words: film (入圍/頒獎), steel (鋼雕/保險箱).'
   "入圍 means being nominated; 頒獎 means presenting the awards. 星光大道 is the red carpet before the ceremony. 鋼雕 is sculpture made of steel; 保險箱 is the safe that holds Kaohsiung's labour memories."
   'The ceremony starts at 18:30 on Nov 22.'
   'Memory trick: learn 入圍 first, then the ceremony （頒獎）, then the place it happens （星光大道）.'
   'B2 · 港台說法 · Local talk'
   "Taiwan and Hong Kong each have their own way of saying things. This week: 打卡 (check in with a photo), 集點 (collecting points), 遊行 (street parade) and 感謝祭 (fans' thanksgiving festival)."
   'Four local words from this issue: 打卡, 集點, 遊行, 感謝祭.'
   "打卡 at a fair means posting a photo to say 'I was here'. 集點 is earning points each time you exercise. 遊行 is the celebration march through the streets; 感謝祭 is the team's thank-you festival for its fans."
   '集點 means collecting points when you exercise.'
   '感謝祭 thanks the fans.'
   "You don't need many local sayings — learn four and every outing feels closer."
